cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. A version-specific DOI
  is issued by Zenodo when the GitHub repository is archived; add the
  "doi" field and the "Concept DOI" here once that DOI exists.
title: >-
  Protocol Choices Can Reverse Rounds-to-Target Rankings in Federated
  Learning -- code and data
abstract: >-
  A measurement study of the protocol used to produce rounds-to-target (RTT)
  rankings in federated learning. On one fixed set of 294 training traces
  (7 methods x 7 dataset/heterogeneity cells x 6 seeds), the identity of the
  fastest algorithm changes with the target accuracy, the global
  learning-rate decay moves inter-method gaps by roughly an order of
  magnitude, and the statistic used to decide "reached" is biased toward
  unstable methods. The repository ships the traces, a systematic
  reporting-practice survey of 58 studies, and one command per table and
  figure.
